00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:52.018
final season.
-Yes.

00:00:52.018 --> 00:00:53.919
-And you got to, you know,
come back

00:00:53.919 --> 00:00:55.455
and play a character that
you played on "The Good Wife."

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:56.756
That must have been so nice.

00:00:56.756 --> 00:00:58.558
-It was really lovely, actually.
I'm so glad I did it,

00:00:58.558 --> 00:00:59.859
because when I did it,
I didn't know it was

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:01.360
going to be the last season.
-Yeah.

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:03.663
-And so I'm really glad
I've kind of gotten back.

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:05.031
And I was so nice to go back.

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:07.266
It was in the same studio,
it was a lot of the same people.

00:01:07.266 --> 00:01:09.436
My daughter -- Sarah Steele,
who plays my daughter,

00:01:09.436 --> 00:01:11.971
it was lovely to do stuff
with her again

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:14.507
and also to play --
and also to get to swear.

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:16.442
Because in "The Good Wife,"

00:01:16.442 --> 00:01:18.144
that was on CBS,
so you weren't allowed to swear.

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:21.214
And of course, I sort of thought
inside my head sweary words

00:01:21.214 --> 00:01:22.782
all the time
when I was playing him,

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:23.916
but I could never
actually say them.

00:01:23.916 --> 00:01:26.953
So I got to say
the most awful things.

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:28.287
Yeah.
-Well, they sound --

00:01:28.287 --> 00:01:29.422
they sound very lovely
coming from you.

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:31.191
-Yeah, I liked it.
-So nice job.

00:01:31.191 --> 00:01:33.192
-You have a fascinating role

00:01:33.192 --> 00:01:35.761
in a documentary coming out
called "My Old School."

00:01:35.761 --> 00:01:37.764
-Oh, yes, yes.
It's out, actually. It's out.

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:39.631
It's really good.
It's called "My Old School,"

00:01:39.631 --> 00:01:41.167
and it's -- I play --

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:44.737
like, I lipsync
the person who it's about

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:46.372
because they didn't want
to be seen in it.

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:49.842
So they did an audio interview,
and then so I lip sync them.

00:01:49.842 --> 00:01:52.611
And what is bizarre
is that 25 years ago,

00:01:52.611 --> 00:01:53.879
I was going to do a film,

00:01:53.879 --> 00:01:57.183
a drama, a narrative film
and play that person.

00:01:57.183 --> 00:01:58.617
-And this is the person --

00:01:58.617 --> 00:02:00.920
This is a fairly famous story
about a 32-year-old

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:02.188
who went to...

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:04.290
-So he was -- there's a school
in Glasgow

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:05.291
called Bearsden Academy.

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:07.159
It's a sort of posh area
of Glasgow.

00:02:07.159 --> 00:02:08.862
And he went there,
and then he became --

00:02:08.862 --> 00:02:11.364
went to be a doctor and flunked.

00:02:11.364 --> 00:02:14.099
And then he had to go.
He wanted to be a doctor again,

00:02:14.099 --> 00:02:18.505
but there was a cutoff at age 34
to get back into medical school.

00:02:18.505 --> 00:02:22.241
So he went back to the same
high school that he'd gone to

00:02:22.241 --> 00:02:25.211
when he was 16
and did his exams again

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:26.612
in order to get
into medical school.

00:02:26.612 --> 00:02:28.781
And the same teachers
were teaching him.

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:31.784
-And he was pretending to be 16?
-He was pretending to be 16.

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:33.986
He was pretending to be
this person from Canada

00:02:33.986 --> 00:02:36.388
whose father -- mother
was an opera singer who died.

00:02:36.388 --> 00:02:37.690
And it was, like,
this hilarious,

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:40.192
camp sort of back story.

00:02:40.192 --> 00:02:41.694
And everyone believed it.

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:44.364
And he even went into
the school musical,

00:02:44.364 --> 00:02:45.464
and it was "South Pacific,"

00:02:45.464 --> 00:02:47.533
and he sang
"Younger Than Springtime."

00:02:47.533 --> 00:02:49.335
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.335 --> 00:02:51.136
And nobody -- and nobody
caught him doing it.

00:02:51.136 --> 00:02:53.139
I mean, all the kids sort of
called him 30-something

00:02:53.139 --> 00:02:54.340
and stuff like that.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:55.775
And it's a hilarious bit.
Go, "Are you my Dad?"

00:02:55.775 --> 00:02:59.278
And they're all doing that,
but nobody actually realized.

00:02:59.278 --> 00:03:01.780
And then when it did come out,
oh, my God, it was the huge --

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:04.283
And remember,
in sort of '93, '94.

00:03:04.283 --> 00:03:06.251
it was this huge story
because in Scotland, like,

00:03:06.251 --> 00:03:08.420
we don't like having the wool
pulled over our eyes.

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:11.591
But -- and we also
admire people who can.

00:03:11.591 --> 00:03:14.126
So it was just we were all like,
"What?!"

00:03:14.126 --> 00:03:16.562
And it was just
an immense story.

00:03:16.562 --> 00:03:18.665
So it was kind of nice for me
as well to come

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:20.966
all those years later
to sort of play him.

00:03:20.966 --> 00:03:22.535
It's not
an attractive role for me.

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:23.736
I don't know
if you've seen the poster.

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:24.904
-I haven't seen the poster
for it yet.

00:03:24.904 --> 00:03:26.338
-It's not attractive.
-Okay.

00:03:26.338 --> 00:03:28.975
-But, um...it was a great thing.
-Thank you for the warning.

00:03:28.975 --> 00:03:30.376
-Yes. Just to --

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:33.479
You're also --
you're working with my queen.

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:34.546
This is my queen,
Miriam Margolyes.

00:03:34.546 --> 00:03:36.081
-Oh, my God, Miriam. Yes.

00:03:36.081 --> 00:03:39.619
-So this is -- she's one of the
funniest people in the world.

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:41.053
A wonderful actor.
-So hilarious.

00:03:41.053 --> 00:03:42.955
So we this show in Britain --

00:03:42.955 --> 00:03:44.523
it's on PBS as well, actually,
I think here.

00:03:44.523 --> 00:03:46.892
It's called "Alan and --"
no, "Miriam and Alan,"

00:03:46.892 --> 00:03:48.928
that's the billing.

00:03:48.928 --> 00:03:50.896
"Miriam and Alan
Lost in Scotland" --

00:03:50.896 --> 00:03:52.231
we did one last year,
and now we've done --

00:03:52.231 --> 00:03:53.499
we're in the middle of doing
a second one --

00:03:53.499 --> 00:03:56.135
"Miriam and Alan
Lost in Scotland and Beyond."

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:58.404
So next week, we meet up
again in California.

00:03:58.404 --> 00:03:59.472
-Oh, wow.
-We go to California.

00:03:59.472 --> 00:04:02.208
But this is us
at Loch Lomond last week,

00:04:02.208 --> 00:04:04.310
where I officiated a wedding.

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:08.080
And she -- it was like a gay --
a gay couple

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:09.415
who were renewing their vows.

00:04:09.415 --> 00:04:10.716
My second cousin, actually.

00:04:10.716 --> 00:04:14.287
And I and I officiated that.
and Miriam did a reading.

00:04:14.287 --> 00:04:16.722
She read
"The Owl and the Pussycat."

00:04:16.722 --> 00:04:18.157
And I afterwards I said,
"I didn't --

00:04:18.157 --> 00:04:20.259
Who'd have thunk at a gay
wedding would be so much pussy."

00:04:20.259 --> 00:04:21.860
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:28.033
But anyway, she's so hilarious,
and she's 81.

00:04:28.033 --> 00:04:30.602
She's so foulmouthed,
and like a little girl

00:04:30.602 --> 00:04:32.071
showing her knickers.

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:33.772
And I think where
it kind of become

00:04:33.772 --> 00:04:36.008
this sort of kooky television
couple because I'm so --

00:04:36.008 --> 00:04:37.209
"No, Miriam, stop it."

00:04:37.209 --> 00:04:39.545
But then also
encouraging her to do things.

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:42.614
And she came to see "Burn"
when we were in Inverness,

00:04:42.614 --> 00:04:44.984
and all the crew
were so excited to meet her.

00:04:44.984 --> 00:04:46.419
You know, she's, like, a legend.

00:04:46.419 --> 00:04:48.887
And she came into -- they all
came into my dressing room.

00:04:48.887 --> 00:04:50.489
She was sitting there,
and I could tell she was like,

00:04:50.489 --> 00:04:52.091
"Oh, I'm going to have fun
here."

00:04:52.091 --> 00:04:55.194
And she just suddenly went,
"I've realized that I've come

00:04:55.194 --> 00:04:57.496
to agree with Alan
about circumcision."

00:04:57.496 --> 00:04:58.631
They're all like, "What?!"

00:04:58.631 --> 00:05:00.966
[ Laughter ]

00:05:00.966 --> 00:05:03.336
And she goes,
"Because I don't think people

00:05:03.336 --> 00:05:05.471
should be circumcised.
He's quite right.

00:05:05.471 --> 00:05:07.440
You have
a foreskin for a reason."

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:09.041
And I was like,
"Yes, thanks, Miriam.

00:05:09.041 --> 00:05:10.910
Yes, thank you
for your support."

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:12.511
And then she goes, "But you
know, you've got to be

00:05:12.511 --> 00:05:14.680
very aware of the smegma."
I'm like, "Alright!"

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:16.649
[ Laughter ]

00:05:16.649 --> 00:05:18.818
And that's where go goes.
She starts in something,

00:05:18.818 --> 00:05:20.186
and you think, "Oh, what is she
going on about?"

00:05:20.186 --> 00:05:22.454
And then she made this gesture.
I went, "Okay, Miriam,

00:05:22.454 --> 00:05:24.089
that's enough."
And she went, "No,

00:05:24.089 --> 00:05:26.158
but some people store it."

00:05:26.158 --> 00:05:28.594
Like that, and she made
this gesture like a shovel,

00:05:28.594 --> 00:05:32.098
and I was like, "Do you mean,
like, shoveling smegma?

00:05:32.098 --> 00:05:33.266
Is that what you're doing here?"

00:05:33.266 --> 00:05:36.002
And she went,
"Yes, that's what they do."

00:05:36.002 --> 00:05:37.570
And so that's
what you're dealing with.

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:38.538
-Just once again, that's who is
saying all that.

00:05:38.538 --> 00:05:40.173
-This lady.

00:05:40.173 --> 00:05:42.508
-That very sweet-looking lady
right there.

00:05:42.508 --> 00:05:45.645
-Oh, and that's one of the
cleanest stories I can tell you.

00:05:45.645 --> 00:05:46.979
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.979 --> 00:05:48.681
-Hey, congratulations
on your show.

00:05:48.681 --> 00:05:50.015
-Thank you.

00:05:50.015 --> 00:05:51.684
-Congratulations on another
season --

00:05:51.684 --> 00:05:53.553
well, just coming back
and doing "The Good Fight."

00:05:53.553 --> 00:05:54.921
And it's so great to have you.
-Just being alive.

00:05:54.921 --> 00:05:57.089
-Alan Cumming, just being alive.

00:05:57.089 --> 00:05:59.725
"Burn" is playing now through
September 25th

00:05:59.725 --> 00:06:00.993
at the Joyce Theater.

00:06:00.993 --> 00:06:02.962
New episodes of the final season
of "The Good Fight"

00:06:02.962 --> 00:06:04.430
are available Thursdays
on Paramount+.

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:06.532
We'll be right back with
Bobby Moynihan.

